# The path-based front door for the public nests (#3028): https://nuthatch-indexer.com/nests/arc-usdc and
# /nests/base-usdc. nuthatch-frontend's vercel.json rewrites each of those paths to one of the two sites
# below, the pattern bounty-nest already uses. A name under sslip.io already resolves to the host and Caddy
# gets its certificate the way it does for any name, so adding a nest never needs a DNS record.
#
#   browser/agent -> Vercel (nuthatch-indexer.com/nests/<id>/...) -> Caddy :443 (this file)
#                 -> nginx (the allowlist and limits, nginx*.conf) -> the nest
#
# Append to Helsinki's /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, with your own host's name for the two sites. Two things differ
# from Caddyfile.arc-testnet, because the caller is Vercel and not the visitor:
#
#  - Host. The nest answers only the name it was told with --public-host, so each site sends that name.
#  - The visitor's address. Every request arrives from one of Vercel's addresses, which differ per request, so
#    nginx would count every visitor as one caller. Vercel puts the visitor's address in X-Vercel-Forwarded-For
#    and overwrites a copy a visitor sends (checked 2026-11-19 by sending spoofed X-Vercel-Forwarded-For,
#    X-Forwarded-For, X-Real-IP and X-Vercel-Proxied-For through a deployment: the nest saw the real address;
#    X-Real-IP is not used here because it did not always get overwritten). When that header holds an address
#    it becomes X-Forwarded-For, which nginx rate-limits on. A request straight to this host has no such
#    header from Vercel, but a caller can add one, and so name the address they are limited under; the
#    per-nest limit on all callers together (`all_query` in nginx.conf) still caps what that can cost.
#    Do not add `trusted_proxies`: Vercel's addresses are not a fixed list.
#
# arc.nuthatch-indexer.com (Caddyfile.arc-testnet) keeps working beside this.
arc-usdc.89.167.109.4.sslip.io {
	request_body {
		max_size 64KB
	}
	@viavercel header_regexp vercel X-Vercel-Forwarded-For ^[0-9a-fA-F:.]{3,45}$
	handle @viavercel {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8480 {
			header_up Host arc.nuthatch-indexer.com
			header_up X-Forwarded-For {http.request.header.X-Vercel-Forwarded-For}
			transport http {
				dial_timeout 2s
				response_header_timeout 20s
			}
		}
	}
	handle {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8480 {
			header_up Host arc.nuthatch-indexer.com
			transport http {
				dial_timeout 2s
				response_header_timeout 20s
			}
		}
	}
}

base-usdc.89.167.109.4.sslip.io {
	request_body {
		max_size 64KB
	}
	@viavercel header_regexp vercel X-Vercel-Forwarded-For ^[0-9a-fA-F:.]{3,45}$
	handle @viavercel {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8481 {
			header_up Host base.nuthatch-indexer.com
			header_up X-Forwarded-For {http.request.header.X-Vercel-Forwarded-For}
			transport http {
				dial_timeout 2s
				response_header_timeout 20s
			}
		}
	}
	handle {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8481 {
			header_up Host base.nuthatch-indexer.com
			transport http {
				dial_timeout 2s
				response_header_timeout 20s
			}
		}
	}
}
